        <p>Catographer is a private walking diary. Distances, durations, explored areas, weather and related statistics are estimates based on device sensors, Apple services and the data you record or import, and may be inaccurate. The App is not intended for legal, medical, emergency, or navigation-critical use.</p>
        <h2>3. Your safety</h2>
        <p>You are solely responsible for your safety and the safety of others when walking, hiking or running. Do not use the App in a way that distracts you from your surroundings, traffic, terrain or weather. Choose routes and conditions suited to your ability, carry means of calling for help, and obey local laws and access rules. The App does not provide turn-by-turn navigation or emergency features and must not be relied on to find your way or to be found.</p>
        <h2>4. Health disclaimer</h2>
        <p>The App is not a medical device and does not provide medical advice, diagnosis or treatment. Consult a qualified professional before starting or changing any physical activity. Any workout data saved to Apple Health is provided as-is.</p>
        <h2>5. User content and backups</h2>
        <p>You retain rights in walks, notes, photos, and other content you create. The App processes that content on your device (and, if you enable iCloud sync, in your private iCloud). You are responsible for backups. Uninstalling the App, changing devices or deleting data may permanently remove local content, and we cannot recover it. You grant us no license to your content, as we do not receive it.</p>
        <h2>6. Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>You agree not to copy, modify, reverse engineer, decompile, or create derivative works of the App, to remove proprietary notices, to circumvent its technical protections, or to use it unlawfully, except where such restrictions are prohibited by applicable law.</p>
        <h2>7. Intellectual property</h2>
        <p>The App, its design, code, name and icons are owned by {DEVELOPER} and protected by intellectual property laws. No rights are granted except the license in section 1. Map data and weather are provided by Apple and remain subject to Apple’s terms.</p>
        <h2>8. Third-party services</h2>
        <p>Optional features may use Apple Maps, Apple Weather, Apple Health, and CloudKit/iCloud. Those services are governed by their own terms and privacy policies, and we are not responsible for their availability or accuracy.</p>
        <h2>9. Disclaimer and limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>The App is provided “as is” and “as available.” To the maximum extent permitted by law, {DEVELOPER} disclaims all warranties, including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, accuracy, and uninterrupted or error-free operation, and is not liable for indirect, incidental or consequential damages, loss of data, or injury or loss arising from your use of the App or from reliance on its information. Nothing in these Terms excludes liability that cannot be excluded by law, including for death or personal injury caused by negligence, fraud, or mandatory consumer rights.</p>
        <h2>10. Termination</h2>
        <p>These Terms apply until terminated. Your license ends automatically if you breach them. You may stop at any time by deleting the App.</p>
        <h2>11. Changes</h2>
        <p>We may update these Terms or the App. The effective date above shows the latest version; continued use after an update means you accept it.</p>
        <h2>12. Apple</h2>
        <p>These Terms are between you and {DEVELOPER}, not Apple. Apple has no obligation to provide maintenance or support for the App, and is not responsible for claims relating to it. Apple and its subsidiaries are third-party beneficiaries of these Terms and may enforce them against you.</p>
        <h2>13. Governing law and disputes</h2>
        <p>These Terms are governed by the laws of the Republic of Lithuania. Disputes shall be submitted to the competent courts of Lithuania, except where mandatory consumer-protection laws of your country of residence give you the right to bring claims in your home courts or provide additional rights.</p>
